**Project gallery** — flexbox, not the grid, so the six items reflow cleanly:

```css
.project-gallery {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 20px;
}
.project-gallery-item {
    flex: 1 1 calc(33.333% - 40px);
    max-width: calc(33.333% - 40px);
    margin: 10px;
    background-color: #f0f0f0;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    text-align: center;
}
```

Three across at 1200px, wrapping as the viewport narrows. Note the `gap: 20px` and the per-item `margin: 10px` are doing overlapping jobs — worth picking one in DevTools rather than carrying both.

**Contact form** — Bootstrap `.form-control` fields for name, email, message, with a submit handler that `preventDefault()`s, checks all three fields are non-empty, alerts and resets on success. That's placeholder-grade validation; if you want it to survive contact with a real user, the next step is Bootstrap's `needs-validation` / `was-validated` classes rather than `alert()`.

